  "codex_last_message": "**Changed**\nAdded configurable ANN geometry support in [src/db.rs](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/src/db.rs:1) via `VDB_SECONDARY_CLUSTERS`, and wired it through [measure_ann_search_only](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/measure_ann_search_only:1), [measure_ann_benchmark](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/measure_ann_benchmark:1), [sweep_ann_search_only](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/sweep_ann_search_only:1), and [sweep_ann_benchmark](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/sweep_ann_benchmark:1). I also updated [campaign_journal.md](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/campaign_journal.md:1), [strategy.md](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/strategy.md:1), [research_notes.md](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/research_notes.md:1), [tools/README.md](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/README.md:1), and added [cycle_048.json](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/recent_cycles/cycle_048.json:1).\n\nI tested geometry-only ANN sweeps and a temporary farthest-first k-means seed. Geometry reduced scan count but wrecked the recall/QPS tradeoff, and the seed change improved local recall without transferring to the exact gate, so that seed branch was reverted. The kept code is the old ANN hot path plus the new geometry/harness support.\n\n**Status**\nSerial validation is clean: `run_correctness_test` passed at `1.0000`, and serial quick `run_benchmark` reached `12222.73 QPS`, `1.0000` recall. Exact fast ANN rechecked at `5310.10 QPS`, `0.9532` recall, so score expectation is still roughly low-`12k` quick on the default scorer and mid-`5k` exact on ANN. I do not expect promotion from this cycle.\n\nNext best move: stop spending time on geometry or centroid seeding alone. The new `--secondary-clusters` knob is useful, but the next credible Rust change still needs a materially stronger shortlist signal, most likely residual-aware cluster-local codebooks or another routing stage that changes the recall curve before scan cost dominates again.",
